  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="86b06e0b-aafd-5d0c-bdd6-880b1b861e75" activityNameId="f9031cd6-7e08-5bc3-937b-b0f117be350e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">MG-silicon, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: MG-silicon, at plant
MG-silicon with a purity of 99%. Used for the production of aluminium compounds, silicones and semiconductors. For the use in semiconductors further purification is necessary.;
CAS number: 7440-21-3; 
Formula: Si; 
Synonyms: metal grade silicon; 
UUID: 04621035-cc46-30a7-8c39-e3f0460da9fb
Gate to gate inventory for production of MG-silicon from silica sand including materials, energy use, wastes and air emissions. Emissions to water are not available.
Location: Generic production efforts with specific electricity mixes.
Technology: Modern technology, waste heat is partly recovered and used for electricity generation and/or district heating.
Time period: Time of investigation
Production volume: 1'000'000t worldwide in 2000. Most of European plants are located in NO.
Sampling: Publication of plant specific data in a European survey. 
Extrapolations: Air emissions of different pollutants are extrapolated from environmental reports.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_04621035-cc46-30a7-8c39-e3f0460da9fb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="d4421e85-4eb7-535c-9a92-4641795139a0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
